    {
      "id": "PhR5RMwy8A8PYqGCJRWye",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1184.3459744079873,
      "y": -57.05326209555653,
      "width": 1552.038818359375,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0D",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 290106332,
      "version": 445,
      "versionNonce": 1617240540,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783615861255,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SSR vs CSR\n- use SSR for the landing page and critical content (for SEO and fast initial load), and then switch to CSR for interactivity as users browse pins and boards.\n- In reality, we could use SSR with hydration (initial pi's markup and data are include in initial HTML without position)\n\nSPA vs MPA\n- MPA: full page navigation will destroy current pages' DOM and feed data store in memory, causing previous scroll to be lost in back button\n- SPA: position is maintain for individual routing\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SSR vs CSR\n- use SSR for the landing page and critical content (for SEO and fast initial load), and then switch to CSR for interactivity as users browse pins and boards.\n- In reality, we could use SSR with hydration (initial pi's markup and data are include in initial HTML without position)\n\nSPA vs MPA\n- MPA: full page navigation will destroy current pages' DOM and feed data store in memory, causing previous scroll to be lost in back button\n- SPA: position is maintain for individual routing\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
