      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783618321522,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "*** Virtualization ***",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*** Virtualization ***",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "PROLVntOKonBOIMmBm0yz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1621.6717666264194,
      "y": 3054.6302404925914,
      "width": 567.17236328125,
      "height": 290.07435561349337,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0r",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 557332956,
      "version": 117,
      "versionNonce": 738580836,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783618556500,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "-- An infinite masonry feed can easily grow to thousands of items in a single session,\n and rendering them all balloons memory, slows reconciliation, \nand makes every reflow expensive. Keep only the pins in and around the viewport mounted \nand recycle the rest; the absolute-positioning layout already fixes the container height, \nso nodes above and below the viewport can be removed without shifting scroll position.\n-- I would first ship non-virtualized masonry with image optimization and pagination. \nIf DOM size becomes a bottleneck, I would add column-level virtualization. \nI would not prematurely add complex virtualization \nunless profiling shows long tasks, memory pressure, or scroll jank.\n-- Virtualize on column level\n1. Maintain cumulative item offsets.\n2. On scroll, find first visible item via binary search.\n3. Render visible items plus overscan.\n4. Use top/bottom spacer or absolute positioning.\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 12.892193582821925,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-- An infinite masonry feed can easily grow to thousands of items in a single session,\n and rendering them all balloons memory, slows reconciliation, \nand makes every reflow expensive. Keep only the pins in and around the viewport mounted \nand recycle the rest; the absolute-positioning layout already fixes the container height, \nso nodes above and below the viewport can be removed without shifting scroll position.\n-- I would first ship non-virtualized masonry with image optimization and pagination. \nIf DOM size becomes a bottleneck, I would add column-level virtualization. \nI would not prematurely add complex virtualization \nunless profiling shows long tasks, memory pressure, or scroll jank.\n-- Virtualize on column level\n1. Maintain cumulative item offsets.\n2. On scroll, find first visible item via binary search.\n3. Render visible items plus overscan.\n4. Use top/bottom spacer or absolute positioning.\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
